Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, their roles, and conditions that will be useful  

• event_date : limits the scan to 20201101‑20201130 (inclusive).  
• event_name : we only want 'purchase'.  
• ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd : must be non‑NULL; holds the purchase revenue per event.  
• user_pseudo_id : user identifier that we finally aggregate on.  
• event_params (ARRAY<STRUCT<key,value…>>) : contains the key = 'ga_session_id' that lets us group every event into its session.  
• event_params.value.int_value : the field that actually stores ga_session_id when key = 'ga_session_id'.  

Typical filters that will be used  
WHERE event_name = 'purchase'  
  AND ecommerce.purchase_revenue_in_usd IS NOT NULL  
  AND _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'  

Below are ten exploratory → analytical queries, each limited to 20 rows, that gradually build up to the final answer.

